.TH DRAW 5
.SH NAME
draw \- drawing file and template
.SH DESCRIPTION
A drawing file, for
.IR smdraw (1)
and
.IR smsheet (1),
is ASCII, in the language of
.IR plicad (7),
with one record a line; the text of a record runs to the end of the
line, and a long one may run on over lines that end in a backslash.
.PP
.RS
.nf
units in|mm [in|mm]
template FILE
scale S
field NAME TEXT
material TEXT
finish TEXT
boxed TEXT
note TEXT
revision REV DATE BY TEXT
inserts FORMAT
hatching GAP
unmarked MATERIAL
unhatched MATERIAL...
view NAME [hidden] [scale S] [sheet N] [at X Y] [cut D] [title TEXT]
.fi
.RE
.PP
The units are required: the dimensions are written in the first, with
the second, if given, after each in brackets (and the template may
show them, as Units).
The template, a file next to the drawing file or in the templates of
the library
.RI ( plicad-lib (7)),
fixes the paper and is
required.
A view with
.B cut
is a section by the plane D along the axis toward the eye from the
origin of the part, in mm unless D says in
.RI ( smview (1)):
the faces cut get section lines, of another angle for each part of an
assembly.
A scale record sets one scale for all views.
A field sets a text listed by the template.
The material is note 1 and the finish note 2, both with boxed numbers;
.B boxed
adds a further note with a boxed number, and
.B note
one without.
In notes, %%t is the sheet thickness and %%r the inside bend radius.
An inserts record sets the callout of each group of inserts of one type
on one side, as
.B "inserts %n X %t, INSTALL %s SIDE"
.RI ( smdim (1)).
An unhatched record names the materials whose coats get no hatch, as
.B "unhatched blackjack"
for a powder coat beside masked surfaces that are hatched; without one,
each coat that is a rectangle gets one.
A hatching record sets the gap between the section lines of the
faces a section cuts, on the paper, in mm unless it says in
.RB ( .08in
without one).
After the notes comes a note for each texture of the coats in the views,
.B "TEXTURE: CALLOUT ON SURFACES MARKED"
and the mark in quotes, as
.BR "TEXTURE: VDI 3400 REF 30 ON SURFACES MARKED \(dqT\(dq" ;
a mark stands once in a view on the faces of its texture
.RI ( smdim (1)),
and no two textures share one
.RI ( smview (1)).
Where every face has a texture and there are two or more, one marks
none, the one that the record
.B unmarked
names, or else the one of the most area; its note comes last, as
.BR "TEXTURE: ALL OTHER SURFACES SPI B-3" .
Lines beginning with a blank belong to the view above, records for
.IR smdim (1):
.PP
.RS
.nf
drop FEATURE [x|y|d|r]
lin x|y A B [PLUS MINUS]
leader X Y TEXT
flag X Y N [TEXT]
hatch X0 Y0 X1 Y1
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B drop
leaves out the dimensions of a feature of the part, a name of its
source
.RI ( sm (5)):
all of them, or its ordinates on one axis, its hole callouts or its
radii.
Lengths are from the datum of the view, the lower left corner, at full
size, in mm unless they say
.BR in ;
so is
.B at
of a view, from the lower left corner of the sheet.
Each boxed note needs a flag record under some view.
.PP
A template is PostScript that draws the border, title block and
revision table of one paper, in inches, with the regions given in
comments:
.PP
.RS
.nf
%%PliCadPaper: W H
%%PliCadRoom: X0 Y0 X1 Y1
%%PliCadKeep: X0 Y0 X1 Y1
%%PliCadNotes: X0 Y0 X1 Y1
%%PliCadRevisions: X0 X1 TOP ROW
%%PliCadFields: NAME ...
.fi
.RE
.PP
Paper and room are required; keep may be repeated.
Notes are wrapped to the width of their region and set from its foot.
The revision table has two heading rows and one row per revision,
each ROW high, downward from TOP.
Before the template, these strings are defined: each listed field
(empty if not set; Filename is the name of the drawing file with its
extension), Paper, Units, Scale, Sheet,
Sheets, MaterialNote, FinishNote, and Revisions, an array of
[REV DATE BY TEXT] (empty except on sheet 1).
The procedures TX, LN and FLG may be used in the template.
TX lays a text out by the widths of osifont, as the notes are wrapped;
where Ghostscript draws it in another font, a wider one, it squeezes
the text along its line to that width, so no text leaves its room.
.SH EXAMPLES
A C template with a title, and a drawing for it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
%%PliCadPaper: 22 17
%%PliCadRoom: 0.9 0.9 21.1 15
%%PliCadFields: Title
[ Title ] 11 16 0 0.2 1 TX

units in
template title_c.ps
field Title BRACKET (L), 2X
view top
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
smdraw(1), smsheet(1), smdim(1)
